
v1.1.0 (13 nov 2026)

Minor release, the first of the release/v1.1 line: Infrabase builds SO3
again, updiff only folds what was really edited, and the deploy and
platform-switch paths are fixed.

	•	SO3 recipes. Infrabase builds SO3 as well as Linux: the kernel,
		usr-so3, its musl 1.2.6 toolchain and bsp-so3, standalone or as an
		AVZ guest, on virt64 and virt32. QEMU's virt machine carries the
		so3 devices (absolute pointer, LAN9118) and st.sh passes a LAN9118
		NIC, which a Linux guest ignores. U-Boot now takes virt64_defconfig
		on every virt64 chain, the bare Linux one included. (#68)

	•	updiff detects edits from the attach manifest instead of diffing
		every patched file against pristine: after a git pull bringing new
		patches, an updiff about an unrelated file no longer reverts them.
		Successive patches of one edited file are merged, an emptied patch
		goes away, and updiff refuses to write when the series changed
		under the tree. It folds edits into every series a recipe applies,
		caps the number of new files (IB_UPDIFF_MAX_NEW) and refuses BSP
		recipes. (#64/#66, #67, #70)

	•	Platform switch: buildroot reconfigures, and drops its previous
		output, when IB_PLATFORM or its defconfig changes, and the user
		space CMake cache is wiped on an architecture change. Switching
		virt64 to virt32 used to fail on a missing rootfs.cpio. (#61)

	•	Deploy: the rootfs partition is emptied before the rootfs goes onto
		it, so files the build no longer produces do not survive (#65); the
		user space is copied without imposing the builder's ownership on
		/, /etc, /usr and /root (#52); only the storage image's loop
		devices are detached (#66).

	•	Build: avz refetches when its SRCREV or patch set changes, the
		buildroot make is skipped while nothing changed, 32-bit kernels
		build with ARCH=arm, and linux/rootfs/images/initrd.cpio points to
		the board's tracked initrd (#63, #66).

	•	The tezi-custom sources needed by recovery-edgem.sh are committed
		(#69), and the documentation shows the release under the sidebar
		title (#62).

v1.0.1 (2 oct 2026)

Patch release on the release/v1.0 line: four fixes to v1.0.0.

	•	deploy.sh can redeploy just the kernel. "deploy.sh linux" failed,
		since no kernel recipe had a deploy task; the kernel recipes now
		hand over to their BSP, which repacks the ITB and writes it onto
		the boot partition without compiling anything ("deploy.sh
		usr-zephyr" for a Zephyr image). The partial Linux boot deploy also
		used to write the ITB of the previous full build: a rebuilt kernel
		never reached the card. A kernel that was never built for the
		platform is now reported by name instead of failing inside
		mkimage. (#54, #56)

	•	AVZ on the Raspberry Pi 4 (rpi4_64): the agency took an EL2 data
		abort as soon as the network started, because the hypervisor
		indexed a 160-entry interrupt array with BCM2711 interrupt numbers
		up to 208. The avz recipe follows the SO3 fix (so3#334) until SO3
		tags a release carrying it. (#53)

	•	QEMU is no longer rebuilt from scratch by every "build.sh qemu".
		The configure step re-ran each time, and QEMU's configure starts by
		deleting its build directory; it now runs only when the target list
		or the options change, and the build is incremental. (#57)

	•	U-Boot stays at its prompt when no OS has been deployed. With
		U-Boot alone on the boot partition there is no uEnv.txt, and the
		boot command imported whatever lay in memory, then failed on an
		undefined "start". The QEMU boot command also imports uEnv.txt
		with its exact length now, as the Raspberry Pi one did. (#58)

v1.0.0 (26 sep 2026)

First release of Infrabase, and the first line with a release branch
(release/v1.0). It is the build system the SO3, EDGE-M1, MICOFE and course
trees are aligned on, as it stood once that alignment was done.

	•	A minimal Linux system built with BitBake: U-Boot, the kernel, a
		buildroot root filesystem and the user-space applications, for QEMU
		virt64 and virt32, the Raspberry Pi 4 (64 and 32-bit), the Toradex
		Verdin iMX8M Plus and x86 QEMU. Components are fetched from upstream
		and patched from tracked patch sets; the attach guard refuses to
		overwrite local edits, and updiff folds them back into the set.

	•	The boot chain is one ordered value, IB_BOOT_CHAIN, over the stages
		atf, optee, uboot, avz and mcuboot: Linux on a bare U-Boot, with ATF,
		with an OP-TEE secure world, or as a guest of the AVZ hypervisor at
		EL2. The order is checked, everything else (IB_HYPERVISOR, the stage
		flags, the ITS) is derived from it, and each platform declares the
		stages it can run, so an impossible combination is refused at parse
		time.

	•	Deployment to an SD-card image, a real device or a Toradex Easy
		Installer network feed served from the tree. The deploy writes
		filesystem/boot.conf, and st.sh starts QEMU from it. On virt64 U-Boot
		can be read off the card by the QEMU boot ROM
		(IB_FIRST_STAGE_FROM_CARD). The user space goes where the running
		root is: into the ramfs, or onto the rootfs partition.

	•	A containerised build environment (dbuild.sh): the cross toolchains and
		every host package in one image, the tree bind-mounted, the build run
		as the calling user.

	•	Every script prints the release it belongs to when it starts,
		"[infrabase v1.0.0] build.sh bsp-linux", from the git tag
		(scripts/ibversion.sh); the documentation derives its version from the
		same helper.
